                    <msContents><!-- describe the intellectual content of an inscription -->
                        <summary>This inscription cites the rulership of three different Kalyana Calukya kings, beginning with Tailapa II. The section dealing with Tailapa II's rule states that he performed Brahmanda Kratu in the first year of his reign upon which
                            Revaya-dvedi Cattopadhyaya Somayaji of the Kasyapa gotra received village of modeyanur as a gift, free of imposts. He in turn bestowed the village on a group of twenty Brahmans, along with grants for the maintainance and rituals of the temple of Traipurusa. 
                            The details of the grant are largely effaced and the digital edition has been prepared from P.B. Desai's edition.  </summary>
                        <!-- offers the possibility to give a summary of the inscription's content -->
                    </msContents>
